{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     unit — NSDS's .ns-unit: one row in a training section's contents.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Emits its own <li>, because .ns-units is a <ul> upstream and a bare <a>
     inside a list is invalid markup that also loses the row's spacing.

     PARAMETERS
       currentSlug   slug of the page being viewed, so the row can mark
                     itself. Passed in rather than reached for: inside a
                     {{#get}} → {{#foreach}} the path back is a stack of `../`
                     that changes the moment the nesting does.

     ONLY TWO STATES ARE HONEST. Ghost has no per-member progress, so it
     cannot know whether a reader has COMPLETED something. NSDS draws a
     filled check for `done` and an empty circle otherwise; an empty circle is
     the truthful one here, and the filled check is reserved for the day
     there is somewhere real to read completion from.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<li>
    <a class="ns-unit" href="{{url}}"{{#match slug currentSlug}} aria-current="page"{{/match}}>
        <i class="ph ph-circle ns-unit__check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="ns-unit__title">{{title}}</span>
        <span class="ns-unit__type sp-optional">{{~> "internal/format"~}}</span>
        <span class="ns-unit__time sp-duration sp-optional">{{~> "internal/duration"~}}</span>
    </a>
</li>
